  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "El ciclorama del amanecer",
    "overview": "The page is one continuous lit backdrop, like a theater cyclorama at dawn. The top is the last hour of night over the sea at Cabo Corrientes; as you scroll the light rises through a cobalt horizon band, then dawn pink, then peach, until it reaches full morning day. Every section begins in the color the previous one ended in, so there are no hard cuts between sections, only the sky changing. The footer runs the sequence backwards and returns to night.\n\nThe world is made of light, not objects. Its only ornament is a thin horizon line with a pink-peach glow that gathers once when the page loads. Type is a single grotesque (Archivo) at large sizes in sentence case for headings, with spaced uppercase small labels and tabular numerals for times, dates and distances. Photographs are real and sit square-cornered-but-softened (4px) on the gradient. Action is pink on the night and cobalt on the day.\n\nThe world rejects the Airbnb-style listing template, the earlier black-and-gold luxury site, and the nautical-chart direction it replaced.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One unbroken vertical sky gradient: noche, cobalto, violeta, rosa, durazno, día, and back to noche in the footer.",
      "Action color follows the light: rosa on dark ground, cobalto on light ground.",
      "A single ornament: the horizon line with its glow.",
      "One family, Archivo, from 12px labels to 96px display; tabular numerals everywhere.",
      "A fixed sun rail on the right where the sun rises and the clock advances (05:52 to 09:30) with scroll."
